{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"8c5b8f3bcc08f981","type":"text","text":"Who is the god of this age?","x":-1950,"y":-200,"width":320,"height":60},
		{"id":"aa75f32c3cedb98c","type":"text","text":"Introduction","x":-1558,"y":-440,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3ab19d7428a83c2b","type":"text","text":"The passage in context","x":-1558,"y":-360,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ae593748163f859d","type":"text","text":"Moses spoke to Israel with his face uncovered","x":-1558,"y":-280,"width":250,"height":60},
		{
			"id":"e13cee869b5e85b1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Paul calls the covenant on stone a ministry of death",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1560,
			"y":-160,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"679b9a9cd46fdc89",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Paul moves the veil from Moses' face onto minds",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1560,
			"y":-60,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"61e227a96bb30d70",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The god who blinds is the god of that covenant",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1560,
			"y":40,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4f7d069fc4519893",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yhwh is still veiling people",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1560,
			"y":160,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"1135f7b29fb50c8f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The disputed words are in 2 Corinthians 4:4.\nPaul says the God of this age blinded the minds of unbelievers so they can't see the light of the gospel. Modern commentaries say that's Satan. Paul doesn't say Satan. He writes a title, once, and never uses it again anywhere in his letters. So whoever this is has to be identified from the argument around the verse - and that argument is about Moses the covenant carved on stone and a veil.  it's about Yahweh from the first line to the last.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-3040,
			"width":560,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"1bec94f2a1a17f83",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So why does the answer come back Satan? Because of what the alternative would mean. If Yahweh is Jesus' father, Paul can't be pointing at Yahweh here, because that would make the father the one blinding people against his own son. The name gets decided before the passage is read in context.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-2780,
			"width":540,
			"height":170
		},
		{
			"id":"c834b627471b5f0f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The chapter break lands in the middle of Paul's argument. Second Corinthians 4:1 opens with \"therefore\" and carries straight on with the same ministry, the same veil, the same minds, the same glory, the same light, and the same face.  2 Corinthians 2:14 through 4:6 is one argument, and the god in 4:4 creates a major problem: It clearly means Yahweh, but we're not allowed to say that anymore.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-2580,
			"width":530,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"f45fa8407f8353e2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Paul wrote second Corinthians around the year 55 to a church in Ecclesia he had started himself in Corinth. It's a personal letter, because rival teachers were challenging his authority, and he answers them by comparing two ministries - his own, which he calls the ministry of the pneuma, the ministry of the spirit and the one carved on stone.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-2360,
			"width":520,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"76f767875879a11d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"His criticism doesn't come didn't come from outside the covenant system. Paul calls himself a Pharisee, a Hebrew of Hebrews, blameless under the law (which is quite a claim). The man who calls the stone covenant a ministry of death had once treated his record under that law as the best thing about him.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-2160,
			"width":510,
			"height":150
		},
		{
			"id":"2a63d0fe4c5ce61e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Philippians 3:5-6: I was circumcised on the eighth day, from the people of Israel in the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews. I lived according to the law as a Pharisee. In my zeal for theos (Yahweh) I persecuted the ekklesia. According to the righteousness stipulated in the law, I was blameless.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-330,
			"y":-2160,
			"width":540,
			"height":150
		},
		{
			"id":"bb98747c6828225d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"He also came into the Jesus movement as its persecutor. Acts 9:3-9 says the change started with a light so bright it left him unable to see for three days. So the man writing about blinded minds had been blinded by light himself.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-1990,
			"width":500,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"cbf88f9f51f51129",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Who does Paul actually name 2 Corinthians 4:4",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-1830,
			"width":510,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fd10bf19ea11471e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Christianity never settled who the god of this age is",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1260,
			"y":-1760,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"7e119a9ae66ce413",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What is the argument around the verse about?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-1755,
			"width":510,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"78cd403829119328",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Did anyone before Paul use the title \"the god of this age\", and who do they mean by it?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-1680,
			"width":510,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"b27ad5104058b239",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Who does the Bible say blinds and hardens people?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-1580,
			"width":510,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f28ca19fe20ab06c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Why has the answer come back Satan for 400 years?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-1500,
			"width":520,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"012588f6c197f210",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"If the God who blinds in 2 Corinthians 4:4 is not the theos who shines in 2 Corinthians 46, how many gods are on the page?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-1420,
			"width":520,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"0ee08951783de70b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The theos of this age.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-330,
			"y":-1420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6f2e7872418c439a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Satan is the only answer left if Yhwh is Jesus' Father",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1260,
			"y":-1680,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"adbd55605df85597",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The chapter break was added eleven hundred years after Paul wrote",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1260,
			"y":-1600,
			"width":260,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"a33bb2121cf2d5ba",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Paul knew the covenant system from inside",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1260,
			"y":-1490,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c534b1dfe8c5ee96",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Questions that needs an answer",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1260,
			"y":-1410,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f0b6f5d640432daf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"theos (thee-OSS)\nUsually translated: Gog, god\nAny being ragarded as devine - a Greek god, Israel's Elohim, a ruler, an idol, or an adversary",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-922,
			"y":-1315,
			"width":520,
			"height":110
		},
		{
			"id":"50c1ed3848625e5a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"kyrios (KEE-ree-oss)\nUsually translated: Lord, lord, master, sir\nAnyone holding authority, and the work the Greek Old Testament puts whereever the Hebrew has Yhwh.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-1190,
			"width":515,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"a81787bd8e7d7634",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"christos (khree-STOS)\nUsually translated: Christ\nAnointed one: somebody appointed to a role by being anointed.  A title, not a name",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-1060,
			"width":510,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"1547c2c3d82cd622",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"pneuma (PNYOO-mah)\nUsually translated: Spirit, spirit, wind, breath\nBreath, wind, or an unseen animating force, in a person or otherwise.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-950,
			"width":510,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"3155fc2a9eec99ca",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"logos (LOG-oss)\nUsually translated: Word, word\nSomething said, or the reasoning behind it - a statement, an account, an ordering intelligence",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-835,
			"width":510,
			"height":110
		},
		{
			"id":"ded1a6be1730d4f9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"katargeo (kat-ar-GEH-oh)\nUsually translated: fading, abolished, done away with\nTo make something stop working: cancel it, void it, put an end to it.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-720,
			"width":510,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"d642c90148d05eb0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"noema (NO-ay-mah)\nUsually translated: minds, thoughts\nThe mind, or what a mind produces - a thought, a plan, a scheme.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-570,
			"width":510,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"b410903b7d3ae1b7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"atenizo (at-en-EE-zoh)\nUsually translated: look intently, gaze, fix the eyes on\nTo stare at something fixedly rather than glance at it.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-460,
			"width":510,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"8615043fba9d5e6b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yhwh (YAH-weh)\nUsually translated: the LORD\nThe four-consonant personal name of the covenant god. A name, not a title.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-350,
			"width":510,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"1ea1c154ba4523aa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Elohim (eh-loh-HEEM)\nUsually translated: God, gods\nA category word for a divine being, singular or plural depending on the context.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-917,
			"y":-210,
			"width":510,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"bbee91a91e6c9789",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Words left in the original language",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1257,
			"y":-1290,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"804e2766ab8e451f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exodus 34:29-35",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1257,
			"y":-60,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b81b58e9a8fb2c7f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exodus 34:29-32: Now when Moses came down from Mount Sinai with the two tablets of the testimony in his hand - when he came down from the mountain, Moses did not know that the skin of his face shone while he talked with him. When Aaron (Yahweh) and all the Israelites saw Moses, the skin of his face shone; and they were afraid to approach him. But Moses caught to them. So Aaron and all the leaders of the community came back to him, and Moses spoke to them. After this all the Israelites approached, and he commanded them all that Yhwh had spoken to him on Mount Sinai.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":-60,
			"width":600,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"8143ea14dcb527e8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exodus 34:33-35: When Moses finished speaking with them, he would put a veil on his face. But when Moses went in before Yhwh to speak with him, he would remove the veil until he came out. Then he would come out and tell the Israelites what he had been commanded. When the Israelites would see the face of Moses, that the skin of Moses' face shone, Moses would put the veil on his face again, until he went in to speak with Yhwh.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-920,
			"y":190,
			"width":600,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"6bcc52f3514f634b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"2 Cordinthians 2:14-4:6",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1257,
			"y":410,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{"id":"b5e85decf90f1c2b","type":"text","text":"Introduction\n![[Who2 is the god of this age - Introduction#Introduction]]","x":320,"y":-490,"width":480,"height":240},
		{
			"id":"d227067d9b4bd4d5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Source:** Biblical canon\n**Lens:** Independent (Israel Anderson)",
			"styleAttributes":{"border":"invisible","shape":"pill","textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1950,
			"y":-120,
			"width":320,
			"height":60,
			"color":"4"
		}
	],
